module

public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsAlgClosed.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FundamentalGroup.FiniteEtaleOverLimit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FundamentalGroup.FiniteEtaleAlgClosedExtension
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Limits.DescendingMorphisms.Etale
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Limits.DescendingMorphisms.Finite
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Limits.OverPullbackId
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ObjectDescent.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Henselian.Henselization.AlgebraicInCompletion

/-!
# Spreading out a finite étale cover over an extension of algebraically closed fields

Let `k ⊆ k'` be an extension of **algebraically closed** fields and let `X` be proper over `k`.
This file carries out the filtered-colimit argument of Stacks Tag 0A49 that
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FundamentalGroup.FiniteEtaleAlgClosedExtension` leaves as the
hypothesis `AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteEtaleDescendsToHenselianPoint`: every scheme finite étale over
`X_{k'}` is already the base change of one finite étale over `X_R`, for `R` a henselian local
`k`-algebra with residue field `k` mapping to `k'` (an `AlgebraicGeometry.HenselianPoint`).

Discharging that hypothesis turns the conditional Tag 0A49 of that file into Tag 0A49 carrying
only the *proper* case of Tag 0A48 — `AlgebraicGeometry.ProperHenselianFiniteEtaleEquivalence`,
which needs Grothendieck existence over a complete Noetherian ring together with Artin
approximation and is not treated here.

## The argument

* `k'` is the filtered colimit of the subalgebras `k[s]` it generates over its finite subsets
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.isColimitSubalgebraCocone`), so `Spec k'` is the cofiltered limit of the
  `Spec k[s]`, and base changing along `f : X ⟶ Spec k` presents `X_{k'}` as the cofiltered limit
  of the `X_{k[s]}` (`AlgebraicGeometry.isLimitBcCone`).  Each stage is quasi-compact and
  quasi-separated, being of finite type over a Noetherian ring, and the transition morphisms are
  affine.
* A finite étale cover of `X_{k'}` is of finite presentation, so Tag 01ZM descends it to a cover
  of some `X_{k[s]}`; Tag 01ZO makes the descended morphism finite and Tag 07RP makes it étale at
  a later stage, and one stage serves for both because the index category is cofiltered.  This is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finiteEtale_model`.
* Since `k` is algebraically closed and `k[s]` is of finite type, `Spec k[s]` has a `k`-point; the
  henselization `R` of the local ring there is a henselian local `k`-algebra with residue field
  `k`, and the embedding of that local ring into `k'` extends to `R` because `R` is algebraic over
  it (Tag 0A1W) and `k'` is algebraically closed.  This is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.HenselianPoint.exists_factorization_of_finiteType`, and it makes the
  projection `X_{k'} ⟶ X_{k[s]}` factor through `X_R`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_swap_factorization`).
* Pulling the descended cover back from `X_{k[s]}` to `X_R` therefore gives a cover whose base
  change to `X_{k'}` is the one we started from.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.finiteEtaleDescendsToHenselianPoint_of_isAlgClosed` — the spreading-out
  hypothesis of Tag 0A49, with nothing carried, for `k ⊆ k'` algebraically closed and `X` proper
  over `k`.
* `isEquivalence_finiteEtaleBaseChange_specMap_algebraMap_of_properHenselian_of_isAlgClosed`, in
  the same namespace — Tag 0A49 for such an extension, carrying only
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ProperHenselianFiniteEtaleEquivalence`.

## Implementation notes

Mathlib's base-change functor `CategoryTheory.Over.pullback f` sends an object `Z ⟶ Spec k` to the
*second* projection of `Z ×_{Spec k} X`, so the inverse system and its limit cone are built with
the `Spec` factor first, whereas `AlgebraicGeometry.HenselianPoint.baseChangeMap` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteEtaleDescendsToHenselianPoint` put `X` first.  The two conventions are
reconciled once, at the end of
`AlgebraicGeometry.finiteEtaleDescendsToHenselianPoint_of_isAlgClosed`, by transporting along
`CategoryTheory.Limits.pullbackSymmetry`; everything in between is stated in the `Spec`-first
convention, which keeps the limit constructions literal composites of Mathlib functors with no
commutation left to check.

The index category is `Finset k'` rather than the poset of finite-type subalgebras of `k'`: the
subalgebra generated by a finite set is of finite type, every finite-type subalgebra is of that
form, and the filtered-colimit criterion
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Types.FilteredColimit.isColimitOf'` is immediate for this indexing.

`CategoryTheory.isConnected_of_hasTerminal` is installed as a local instance so that the
forgetful functor of an over category is seen to preserve the limits over `(Finset k')ᵒᵖ`, which
has `∅` as a terminal object.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A49](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A49)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A48](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A48)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ZM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ZM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ZO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ZO)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07RP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07RP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A1W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A1W)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### A henselian point of `k'/k` attached to a finite subset of `k'` -/

namespace HenselianPoint

/-- A nontrivial algebra of finite type over an algebraically closed field has a point with
values in that field: a maximal ideal has finite-type, hence finite, residue algebra, and a
finite field extension of an algebraically closed field is trivial. -/
private theorem exists_algHom_of_finiteType (k A : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [CommRing A]
    [Algebra k A] [Algebra.FiniteType k A] [Nontrivial A] : Nonempty (A →ₐ[k] k) := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := Ideal.exists_maximal A
  let : m.IsMaximal := hm
  let : Field (A ⧸ m) := Ideal.Quotient.field m
  let : Algebra.FiniteType k (A ⧸ m) :=
    Algebra.FiniteType.of_surjective (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ k m) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  let : IsJacobsonRing A := isJacobsonRing_of_finiteType (A := k) (B := A)
  let : Module.Finite k (A ⧸ m) := finite_of_finite_type_of_isJacobsonRing k (A ⧸ m)
  have hbij : Function.Bijective (algebraMap k (A ⧸ m)) :=
    IsAlgClosed.algebraMap_bijective_of_isIntegral (k := k) (K := A ⧸ m)
  exact ⟨(AlgEquiv.ofBijective (Algebra.ofId k (A ⧸ m)) hbij).symm.toAlgHom.comp
    (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ k m)⟩

/-- A nontrivial algebraic algebra over an algebraically closed field has a point with values in
that field: the residue algebra at a maximal ideal is an algebraic field extension. -/
private theorem exists_algHom_of_isAlgebraic (k A : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [CommRing A]
    [Algebra k A] [Algebra.IsAlgebraic k A] [Nontrivial A] : Nonempty (A →ₐ[k] k) := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := Ideal.exists_maximal A
  let : m.IsMaximal := hm
  let : Field (A ⧸ m) := Ideal.Quotient.field m
  let : Algebra.IsIntegral k (A ⧸ m) :=
    (inferInstance : Algebra.IsIntegral k A).of_surjective
      (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ k m) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have hbij : Function.Bijective (algebraMap k (A ⧸ m)) :=
    IsAlgClosed.algebraMap_bijective_of_isIntegral (k := k) (K := A ⧸ m)
  exact ⟨(AlgEquiv.ofBijective (Algebra.ofId k (A ⧸ m)) hbij).symm.toAlgHom.comp
    (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ k m)⟩

/-- **A henselization of a local domain inside an algebraically closed field.** If `R` is a local
domain mapping injectively into an algebraically closed field `k'` and `Rh` is a henselization of
`R`, then the map `R → k'` extends to `Rh`.

By Tag 0A1W every element of `Rh` is algebraic over `R`, so `k' ⊗_R Rh` is algebraic over `k'`;
it is nonzero because `Rh` is faithfully flat over `R`, hence has a `k'`-point, and composing with
`Rh → k' ⊗_R Rh` gives the extension. -/
private theorem exists_algHom_of_isHenselization (R Rh k' : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsLocalRing R] [CommRing Rh] [IsLocalRing Rh] [Algebra R Rh] [Field k'] [IsAlgClosed k']
    [Algebra R k'] (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap R k'))
    [IsLocalRing.IsHenselization R (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R) Rh] :
    Nonempty (Rh →ₐ[R] k') := by
  let : FaithfulSMul R k' := (faithfulSMul_iff_algebraMap_injective R k').mpr hinj
  let : Algebra.IsAlgebraic R Rh := ⟨IsLocalRing.isAlgebraic_of_isHenselization R Rh⟩
  let : Module.FaithfullyFlat R Rh :=
    IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.faithfullyFlat (L := IsLocalRing.ResidueField R)
  have hinjTensor : Function.Injective (TensorProduct.mk R Rh k' (1 : Rh)) :=
    Module.FaithfullyFlat.tensorProduct_mk_injective (A := R) (B := Rh) k'
  have hne : (1 : TensorProduct R Rh k') ≠ 0 := fun h => by
    refine one_ne_zero (hinjTensor (a₁ := (1 : k')) (a₂ := 0) ?_)
    simp_all
  let : Nontrivial (TensorProduct R Rh k') := ⟨⟨0, 1, fun h => hne (by simp [h])⟩⟩
  let : Nontrivial (TensorProduct R k' Rh) :=
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.comm R Rh k').symm.toRingEquiv.nontrivial
  let : Algebra.IsAlgebraic k' (TensorProduct R k' Rh) :=
    Algebra.IsAlgebraic.tensorProduct R Rh k'
  obtain ⟨q⟩ := exists_algHom_of_isAlgebraic k' (TensorProduct R k' Rh)
  exact ⟨(q.restrictScalars R).comp Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight⟩

/-- **A henselian local ring between a local domain and an algebraically closed field.** For a
local domain `R` mapping injectively into an algebraically closed field `k'`, some henselization
of `R` admits a map to `k'` over `R`. -/
private theorem exists_henselization_algHom (R k' : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsLocalRing R] [Field k'] [IsAlgClosed k'] [Algebra R k']
    (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap R k')) :
    ∃ (Rh : Type u) (_ : CommRing Rh) (_ : Algebra R Rh) (_ : IsLocalRing Rh)
      (_ : HenselianLocalRing Rh)
      (_ : IsLocalRing.IsHenselization R (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R) Rh),
      Nonempty (Rh →ₐ[R] k') := by
  obtain ⟨Rh, hComm, hAlg, hLocal, hLocalHom, hh, hi, _, hres⟩ := IsLocalRing.exists_henselization R
  let : CommRing Rh := hComm
  let : Algebra R Rh := hAlg
  let : IsLocalRing Rh := hLocal
  let : IsLocalHom (algebraMap R Rh) := hLocalHom
  let : HenselianLocalRing Rh := hh
  have hHens : IsLocalRing.IsHenselization R (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R) Rh :=
    IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.of_ind_etale hh hi
      ⟨RingEquiv.ofBijective (IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map (algebraMap R Rh)) hres,
        fun x => IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map_residue (algebraMap R Rh) x⟩
  let : IsLocalRing.IsHenselization R (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R) Rh := hHens
  exact ⟨Rh, hComm, hAlg, hLocal, hh, hHens, exists_algHom_of_isHenselization R Rh k' hinj⟩

/-- **A henselian point of `k'/k` through which a given finite-type subalgebra factors.** Let
`k ⊆ k'` be an extension of algebraically closed fields and let `A ⊆ k'` be a `k`-subalgebra of
finite type.  Then there is a henselian point `T` of `k'/k`, with underlying ring `R`, and a
`k`-algebra map `A → R` whose composite with `R → k'` is the inclusion `A ⊆ k'`.

Since `k` is algebraically closed and `A` is of finite type, `Spec A` has a `k`-point `p`; let
`R₀ = A_𝔭` be the local ring there, which embeds into `k'` because `A` does and `𝔭` consists of
nonzerodivisors, and let `R` be a henselization of `R₀`.  The residue field of `R` is that of
`R₀`, namely `k`, and the embedding `R₀ → k'` extends to `R` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.HenselianPoint.exists_algHom_of_isHenselization`. -/
private theorem exists_factorization_of_finiteType (k k' : Type u) [Field k] [Field k']
    [Algebra k k'] [IsAlgClosed k] [IsAlgClosed k'] (A : Subalgebra k k')
    [Algebra.FiniteType k A] :
    ∃ (T : HenselianPoint k k') (β : A →+* T.carrier),
      β.comp (algebraMap k A) = algebraMap k T.carrier ∧
        (algebraMap T.carrier k').comp β = A.val.toRingHom := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨p⟩ := exists_algHom_of_finiteType k A
  have hp : Function.Surjective p.toRingHom := fun x => ⟨algebraMap k A x, p.commutes x⟩
  let m : Ideal A := RingHom.ker p.toRingHom
  let : m.IsMaximal := RingHom.ker_isMaximal_of_surjective p.toRingHom hp
  let R := Localization.AtPrime m
  have hAinj : Function.Injective A.val.toRingHom := Subtype.val_injective
  have hg : ∀ y : m.primeCompl, IsUnit (A.val.toRingHom (y : A)) := fun y =>
    isUnit_iff_ne_zero.mpr fun h =>
      y.2 ((map_eq_zero_iff _ hAinj).mp h ▸ m.zero_mem)
  let φ : R →+* k' := IsLocalization.lift hg
  have hφcomp : φ.comp (algebraMap A R) = A.val.toRingHom := IsLocalization.lift_comp hg
  have hRinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A R) :=
    IsLocalization.injective R m.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors
  have hφinj : Function.Injective φ :=
    (IsLocalization.lift_injective_iff hg).2 fun x y =>
      ⟨fun h => by rw [hRinj h], fun h => by rw [hAinj h]⟩
  let : Algebra R k' := φ.toAlgebra
  obtain ⟨H, hcomm, halg, hlocal, hhens, hhh, ⟨c⟩⟩ := exists_henselization_algHom R k' hφinj
  let : CommRing H := hcomm
  let : Algebra R H := halg
  let : IsLocalRing H := hlocal
  let : HenselianLocalRing H := hhens
  let : IsLocalRing.IsHenselization R (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R) H := hhh
  let : IsLocalHom (algebraMap R H) :=
    IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.isLocalHom (L := IsLocalRing.ResidueField R)
  let b : A →+* H := (algebraMap R H).comp (algebraMap A R)
  -- `c` extends `φ`, so `b` and `c` factor the inclusion `A ⊆ k'`.
  have hcb : c.toRingHom.comp b = A.val.toRingHom := by
    ext x
    change c (algebraMap R H (algebraMap A R x)) = A.val x
    rw [AlgHom.commutes]
    exact congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe hφcomp) x
  let : Algebra k H := (b.comp (algebraMap k A)).toAlgebra
  let : Algebra H k' := c.toRingHom.toAlgebra
  let : IsScalarTower k H k' := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x => by
    have h : c (b (algebraMap k A x)) = A.val (algebraMap k A x) := DFunLike.congr_fun hcb _
    change algebraMap k k' x = c (b (algebraMap k A x))
    rw [h, A.val.commutes]
  -- The residue field of `H` is that of `R`, which is `k` by construction of `p`.
  let eR : IsLocalRing.ResidueField R ≃+* k :=
    (IsLocalization.AtPrime.equivQuotMaximalIdeal m R).symm.toRingEquiv.trans
      (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hp)
  let eHR : IsLocalRing.ResidueField R ≃+* IsLocalRing.ResidueField H :=
    RingEquiv.ofBijective (IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map (algebraMap R H))
      (IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.residueField_map_bijective (R := R) (Rh := H))
  have hkey : ∀ x : k, (eHR.symm.trans eR)
      (IsLocalRing.residue H (b (algebraMap k A x))) = x := by
    intro x
    rw [show IsLocalRing.residue H (b (algebraMap k A x))
        = IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map (algebraMap R H)
            (IsLocalRing.residue R (algebraMap A R (algebraMap k A x))) from
      (IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map_residue (algebraMap R H) _).symm]
    change eR (eHR.symm (eHR (IsLocalRing.residue R (algebraMap A R (algebraMap k A x))))) = x
    rw [eHR.symm_apply_apply, show
      IsLocalRing.residue R (algebraMap A R (algebraMap k A x))
        = IsLocalization.AtPrime.equivQuotMaximalIdeal m R
            (Ideal.Quotient.mk m (algebraMap k A x)) from
      (IsLocalization.AtPrime.equivQuotMaximalIdeal_apply_mk m R _).symm]
    change RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hp
      ((IsLocalization.AtPrime.equivQuotMaximalIdeal m R).symm
        (IsLocalization.AtPrime.equivQuotMaximalIdeal m R _)) = x
    rw [AlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply, RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective_apply_mk]
    exact p.commutes x
  have hbij : Function.Bijective ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal H)).comp
      (b.comp (algebraMap k A))) := by
    rw [show (Ideal.Quotient.mk (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal H)).comp (b.comp (algebraMap k A))
        = (eHR.symm.trans eR).symm.toRingHom from RingHom.ext fun x =>
      (eHR.symm.trans eR).injective
        ((hkey x).trans ((eHR.symm.trans eR).apply_symm_apply x).symm)]
    exact (eHR.symm.trans eR).symm.bijective
  exact ⟨{ carrier := H, residue_bijective := hbij }, b, rfl, hcb⟩

/-- **A henselian point of `k'/k` through which a given finite subset of `k'` factors.** The
case of `AlgebraicGeometry.HenselianPoint.exists_factorization_of_finiteType` used below: `A` is
the `k`-subalgebra of `k'` generated by a finite set, which is of finite type. -/
private theorem exists_factorization_of_finset (k k' : Type u) [Field k] [Field k'] [Algebra k k']
    [IsAlgClosed k] [IsAlgClosed k'] (s : Finset k') :
    ∃ (T : HenselianPoint k k') (β : Algebra.adjoin k (s : Set k') →+* T.carrier),
      β.comp (algebraMap k (Algebra.adjoin k (s : Set k'))) = algebraMap k T.carrier ∧
        (algebraMap T.carrier k').comp β =
          (Algebra.adjoin k (s : Set k')).val.toRingHom :=
  have : Algebra.FiniteType k (Algebra.adjoin k (s : Set k')) :=
    (Subalgebra.fg_iff_finiteType _).mp (Subalgebra.fg_adjoin_finset _)
  exists_factorization_of_finiteType k k' _

end HenselianPoint

/-! ### `k'` as the filtered colimit of its finitely generated `k`-subalgebras -/

attribute [local instance] CategoryTheory.isConnected_of_hasTerminal

section Diagram

variable (k k' : Type u) [Field k] [Field k'] [Algebra k k']

/-- The filtered diagram of finitely generated `k`-subalgebras of `k'`, indexed by the finite
subsets of `k'` ordered by inclusion: the finite set `s` is sent to the subalgebra `k[s]` it
generates. -/
private def subalgebraDiagram : Finset k' ⥤ CommRingCat.{u} where
  obj s := CommRingCat.of (Algebra.adjoin k (s : Set k'))
  map h := CommRingCat.ofHom
    (Subalgebra.inclusion (Algebra.adjoin_mono (Finset.coe_subset.mpr (leOfHom h)))).toRingHom

/-- The cocone over `AlgebraicGeometry.subalgebraDiagram` with vertex `k'` whose legs are the
inclusions `k[s] ⊆ k'`. -/
private def subalgebraCocone : Cocone (subalgebraDiagram k k') where
  pt := CommRingCat.of k'
  ι := { app := fun s => CommRingCat.ofHom (Algebra.adjoin k (s : Set k')).val.toRingHom }

/-- **`k'` is the filtered colimit of its finitely generated `k`-subalgebras.** The forgetful
functor to types reflects and preserves this colimit, and on underlying sets the two conditions of
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Types.FilteredColimit.isColimitOf'` are immediate: every element of `k'`
lies in the subalgebra generated by the singleton it spans, and the legs are injective. -/
private noncomputable def isColimitSubalgebraCocone : IsColimit (subalgebraCocone k k') := by
  let := reflectsColimit_of_reflectsIsomorphisms (subalgebraDiagram k k') (forget CommRingCat)
  apply isColimitOfReflects (forget CommRingCat)
  apply Types.FilteredColimit.isColimitOf'
  · intro x
    exact ⟨{x}, ⟨x, Algebra.subset_adjoin (Finset.mem_singleton_self x)⟩, rfl⟩
  · intro i x y h
    exact ⟨i, 𝟙 i, by rw [Subtype.ext h]⟩

/-- The inverse system of affine schemes `Spec k[s]`, indexed by the finite subsets of `k'`. -/
private noncomputable def specDiagram : (Finset k')ᵒᵖ ⥤ Scheme.{u} :=
  (subalgebraDiagram k k').op ⋙ Scheme.Spec

/-- Each `Spec k[s]` is a scheme over `Spec k`, compatibly with the transition morphisms. -/
private noncomputable def specToBase :
    specDiagram k k' ⟶ (Functor.const (Finset k')ᵒᵖ).obj (Spec (.of k)) where
  app i := Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k (Algebra.adjoin k (i.unop : Set k'))))
  naturality i j e := by
    dsimp [specDiagram, subalgebraDiagram]
    rw [← Spec.map_comp]
    simp only [Category.comp_id]
    rw [Spec.map_inj]
    exact CommRingCat.hom_ext (by ext x; rfl)

/-- The inverse system `AlgebraicGeometry.specDiagram` regarded as a diagram of schemes over
`Spec k`. -/
private noncomputable def specOverDiagram : (Finset k')ᵒᵖ ⥤ Over (Spec (.of k)) :=
  Over.lift (specDiagram k k') (specToBase k k')

/-- The cone over `AlgebraicGeometry.specDiagram` with vertex `Spec k'` obtained by applying
`Spec` to `AlgebraicGeometry.subalgebraCocone`. -/
private noncomputable def specCone : Cone (specDiagram k k') :=
  Scheme.Spec.mapCone (subalgebraCocone k k').op

/-- `Spec k'` is the limit of the `Spec k[s]`, because `Spec` turns the colimit
`k' = colim k[s]` into a limit. -/
private noncomputable def isLimitSpecCone : IsLimit (specCone k k') :=
  isLimitOfPreserves _ (isColimitSubalgebraCocone k k').op

/-- The legs of `AlgebraicGeometry.specCone` lie over `Spec k`. -/
private theorem specCone_π_comp (i : (Finset k')ᵒᵖ) :
    (specCone k k').π.app i ≫ (specToBase k k').app i
      = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k k')) := by
  dsimp [specCone, specToBase, specDiagram, subalgebraCocone, subalgebraDiagram]
  rw [← Spec.map_comp, Spec.map_inj]
  exact CommRingCat.hom_ext (by ext x; rfl)

/-- The cone of `AlgebraicGeometry.specOverDiagram` with vertex `Spec k'`, taken in the category
of schemes over `Spec k`. -/
private noncomputable def specOverCone : Cone (specOverDiagram k k') :=
  Over.liftCone (specDiagram k k') (specToBase k k') (specCone k k')
    (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k k'))) (specCone_π_comp k k')

/-- `Spec k'` is the limit of the `Spec k[s]` in the category of schemes over `Spec k`: the index
category is nonempty, so the limit may be computed after forgetting the structure morphism. -/
private noncomputable def isLimitSpecOverCone : IsLimit (specOverCone k k') :=
  have : Nonempty (Finset k')ᵒᵖ := ⟨Opposite.op ∅⟩
  Over.isLimitLiftCone (specDiagram k k') (specToBase k k') (specCone k k') _
    (specCone_π_comp k k') (isLimitSpecCone k k')

end Diagram

/-! ### The base change of the system to `X` -/

section BaseChange

variable (k k' : Type u) [Field k] [Field k'] [Algebra k k']
variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k))

/-- The inverse system `{ Spec k[s] ×_{Spec k} X }` of base changes of
`AlgebraicGeometry.specDiagram` along `f`. -/
private noncomputable def bcDiagram : (Finset k')ᵒᵖ ⥤ Scheme.{u} :=
  specOverDiagram k k' ⋙ Over.pullback f ⋙ Over.forget X

/-- The cone over `AlgebraicGeometry.bcDiagram` with vertex `Spec k' ×_{Spec k} X`. -/
private noncomputable def bcCone : Cone (bcDiagram k k' f) :=
  (Over.pullback f ⋙ Over.forget X).mapCone (specOverCone k k')

/-- **`X_{k'}` is the limit of the `X_{k[s]}`.** Base change along `f` is a right adjoint, hence
preserves limits, and the forgetful functor of an over category preserves limits over a connected
index category. -/
private noncomputable def isLimitBcCone : IsLimit (bcCone k k' f) :=
  isLimitOfPreserves (Over.pullback f ⋙ Over.forget X) (isLimitSpecOverCone k k')

/-- Each stage of `AlgebraicGeometry.bcDiagram` is quasi-compact and quasi-separated: it is of
finite type over the noetherian ring `k[s]`. -/
private theorem bcDiagram_compactSpace_and_quasiSeparatedSpace [IsProper f]
    (i : (Finset k')ᵒᵖ) :
    CompactSpace ((bcDiagram k k' f).obj i) ∧
      QuasiSeparatedSpace ((bcDiagram k k' f).obj i) := by
  let A := Algebra.adjoin k (i.unop : Set k')
  let : Algebra.FiniteType k A :=
    (Subalgebra.fg_iff_finiteType _).mp (Subalgebra.fg_adjoin_finset _)
  let : IsNoetherianRing A := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing k A
  let g : Spec (.of A) ⟶ Spec (.of k) := Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k A))
  let : LocallyOfFiniteType g := by
    rw [HasRingHomProperty.Spec_iff (P := @LocallyOfFiniteType)]
    exact RingHom.finiteType_algebraMap.mpr inferInstance
  let : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace f
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian (pullback g f) :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (pullback.snd g f)
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · change CompactSpace ↥(pullback g f)
    infer_instance
  · change QuasiSeparatedSpace ↥(pullback g f)
    exact IsLocallyNoetherian.quasiSeparatedSpace

/-- The transition morphisms of `AlgebraicGeometry.bcDiagram` are affine: they are base changes
of morphisms of affine schemes. -/
private theorem bcDiagram_isAffineHom {i j : (Finset k')ᵒᵖ} (e : i ⟶ j) :
    IsAffineHom ((bcDiagram k k' f).map e) := by
  change IsAffineHom (((Over.pullback f).map ((specOverDiagram k k').map e)).left)
  refine MorphismProperty.overPullbackMap f ((specOverDiagram k k').map e) ?_
  change IsAffineHom ((specDiagram k k').map e)
  let : IsAffine ((specDiagram k k').obj i) := by
    dsimp [specDiagram, subalgebraDiagram]; infer_instance
  let : IsAffine ((specDiagram k k').obj j) := by
    dsimp [specDiagram, subalgebraDiagram]; infer_instance
  exact isAffineHom_of_isAffine _

end BaseChange

/-! ### Descending a finite étale cover to a finite stage -/

section Model

/-- The base change along `g : T ⟶ S` of a morphism `X₀ ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 S)` in `Over S`, read as an
arrow of schemes, is the structure morphism of the base change of `X₀`. -/
private noncomputable def overPullbackArrowIso {S T : Scheme.{u}} (g : T ⟶ S) {X₀ : Over S}
    {U : Over T} (f₀ : X₀ ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 S)) (e : (Over.pullback g).obj X₀ ≅ U) :
    Arrow.mk (((Over.pullback g).map f₀).left) ≅ Arrow.mk U.hom := by
  let eT := overPullbackIdIso g
  let : IsIso e.hom.left := (Over.forget T).map_isIso e.hom
  let : IsIso eT.hom.left := (Over.forget T).map_isIso eT.hom
  refine Arrow.isoMk (asIso e.hom.left) (asIso eT.hom.left) ?_
  calc e.hom.left ≫ U.hom = ((Over.pullback g).obj X₀).hom := Over.w e.hom
    _ = ((Over.pullback g).map f₀).left ≫ ((Over.pullback g).obj (Over.mk (𝟙 S))).hom :=
        (Over.w ((Over.pullback g).map f₀)).symm
    _ = ((Over.pullback g).map f₀).left ≫ eT.hom.left := by rw [← Over.w eT.hom]; simp

variable (k k' : Type u) [Field k] [Field k'] [Algebra k k']
variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k))

/-! ### The factorization through a henselian point -/

/-- **The projection `X_{k'} ⟶ X_{k[s]}` factors through `X_R` for a henselian point `R`.** The
henselian point is the one produced by
`AlgebraicGeometry.HenselianPoint.exists_factorization_of_finset` from the finite set indexing the
stage, and the factorization is the base change along `f` of the corresponding factorization
`k[s] → R → k'` of rings. -/
private theorem exists_swap_factorization [IsAlgClosed k] [IsAlgClosed k']
    (i : (Finset k')ᵒᵖ) :
    ∃ (T : HenselianPoint k k')
      (l : pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k k'))) f ⟶
        pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k T.carrier))) f)
      (h : pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k T.carrier))) f ⟶
        (bcDiagram k k' f).obj i),
      l ≫ h = (bcCone k k' f).π.app i ∧
        l ≫ pullback.fst (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k T.carrier))) f
            = pullback.fst (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k k'))) f ≫
              Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap T.carrier k')) ∧
          l ≫ pullback.snd (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k T.carrier))) f
            = pullback.snd (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k k'))) f := by
  obtain ⟨T, β, hβk, hβ⟩ := HenselianPoint.exists_factorization_of_finset k k' i.unop
  let B : Over (Spec (.of k)) := Over.mk (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k T.carrier)))
  let βO : B ⟶ (specOverDiagram k k').obj i :=
    Over.homMk (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom β)) (by
      change Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom β) ≫
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
          (algebraMap k (Algebra.adjoin k (i.unop : Set k')))) = B.hom
      rw [← Spec.map_comp, ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp, hβk]
      rfl)
  let γO : (specOverCone k k').pt ⟶ B :=
    Over.homMk (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap T.carrier k'))) (by
      change Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap T.carrier k')) ≫
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k T.carrier)) =
          Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k k'))
      rw [← Spec.map_comp, ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq])
  have hγβ : γO ≫ βO = (specOverCone k k').π.app i := by
    apply Over.OverMorphism.ext
    change Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap T.carrier k')) ≫
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom β) = (specCone k k').π.app i
    rw [← Spec.map_comp, ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp, hβ]
    rfl
  refine ⟨T, ((Over.pullback f).map γO).left, ((Over.pullback f).map βO).left, ?_,
    pullback.lift_fst _ _ _, pullback.lift_snd _ _ _⟩
  change ((Over.pullback f).map γO).left ≫ ((Over.pullback f).map βO).left =
    ((Over.pullback f).map ((specOverCone k k').π.app i)).left
  rw [← hγβ, (Over.pullback f).map_comp]
  rfl

end Model

/-! ### The spreading-out hypothesis, and Tag 0A49 -/

section Descent

variable {k k' : Type u} [Field k] [Field k'] [Algebra k k'] [IsAlgClosed k] [IsAlgClosed k']
variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k))

/-- **The spreading-out hypothesis of Tag 0A49, for an extension of algebraically closed
fields.** Every scheme finite étale over `X_{k'}` is the base change of a scheme finite étale over
`X_R` for some henselian point `R` of `k'/k`.

Write `k'` as the filtered colimit of its finitely generated `k`-subalgebras `k[s]`, so that
`X_{k'}` is the cofiltered limit of the `X_{k[s]}`.  A finite étale cover of `X_{k'}` descends to
one of some `X_{k[s]}` by `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finiteEtale_model`, and the projection
`X_{k'} ⟶ X_{k[s]}` factors through `X_R` for the henselization `R` of `k[s]` at a `k`-point by
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_swap_factorization`; pulling the descended cover back to `X_R` gives the
required cover. -/
theorem finiteEtaleDescendsToHenselianPoint_of_isAlgClosed [IsProper f] :
    FiniteEtaleDescendsToHenselianPoint k k' f := by
  intro Q
  let σ := pullbackSymmetry f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k k')))
  let Q' : FiniteEtaleOver (bcCone k k' f).pt := (finiteEtaleBaseChange σ.inv).obj Q
  letI : ∀ i, CompactSpace ((bcDiagram k k' f).obj i) := fun i =>
    (bcDiagram_compactSpace_and_quasiSeparatedSpace k k' f i).1
  letI : ∀ i, QuasiSeparatedSpace ((bcDiagram k k' f).obj i) := fun i =>
    (bcDiagram_compactSpace_and_quasiSeparatedSpace k k' f i).2
  letI : ∀ {i j : (Finset k')ᵒᵖ} (e : i ⟶ j), IsAffineHom ((bcDiagram k k' f).map e) := fun e =>
    bcDiagram_isAffineHom k k' f e
  obtain ⟨i, V, ⟨e⟩⟩ := AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finiteEtale_model (bcDiagram k k' f)
    (bcCone k k' f) (isLimitBcCone k k' f) Q'
  obtain ⟨T, l, h, hfac, hlfst, hlsnd⟩ := exists_swap_factorization k k' f i
  let τ := pullbackSymmetry f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k T.carrier)))
  have hτ : T.baseChangeMap f ≫ τ.hom = σ.hom ≫ l := by
    apply pullback.hom_ext
    · rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, hlfst, pullbackSymmetry_hom_comp_fst,
        ← Category.assoc, pullbackSymmetry_hom_comp_fst]
      exact pullback.lift_snd _ _ _
    · rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, hlsnd, pullbackSymmetry_hom_comp_snd,
        pullbackSymmetry_hom_comp_snd]
      exact pullback.lift_fst _ _ _
  refine ⟨T, (finiteEtaleBaseChange τ.hom).obj ((finiteEtaleBaseChange h).obj V), ⟨?_⟩⟩
  exact ((finiteEtaleBaseChangeComp (T.baseChangeMap f) τ.hom (σ.hom ≫ l) hτ.symm).app
      ((finiteEtaleBaseChange h).obj V)).symm ≪≫
    (finiteEtaleBaseChangeComp σ.hom l).app ((finiteEtaleBaseChange h).obj V) ≪≫
    (finiteEtaleBaseChange σ.hom).mapIso
      (((finiteEtaleBaseChangeComp l h ((bcCone k k' f).π.app i) hfac.symm).app V).symm ≪≫
        e.symm) ≪≫
    ((finiteEtaleBaseChangeComp σ.hom σ.inv (𝟙 _) σ.hom_inv_id.symm).app Q).symm ≪≫
    finiteEtaleBaseChangeId.app Q

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0A49 for an extension of algebraically closed fields**, granted only
the proper case of Tag 0A48. Let `k ⊆ k'` be algebraically closed fields and let `X` be proper
over `k`.  Then base change `U ↦ U_{k'}` is an equivalence between the category of schemes finite
étale over `X` and the category of schemes finite étale over `X_{k'}`.

This is `isEquivalence_finiteEtaleBaseChange_specMap_algebraMap_of_properHenselian` with its
spreading-out hypothesis discharged by
`AlgebraicGeometry.finiteEtaleDescendsToHenselianPoint_of_isAlgClosed`, applied to each finite
étale cover `P` of `X`, which is again proper over `k`. -/
@[stacks 0A49 "for `k ⊆ k'` algebraically closed, with one input of the source proof carried: \
`ProperHenselianFiniteEtaleEquivalence`, Tag 0A48 for a proper — not merely finite — scheme over \
a henselian local ring. The source's filtered-colimit spreading out is proved here."]
theorem isEquivalence_finiteEtaleBaseChange_specMap_algebraMap_of_properHenselian_of_isAlgClosed
    [IsProper f] (h0A48 : ProperHenselianFiniteEtaleEquivalence.{u}) :
    (finiteEtaleBaseChange (pullback.fst f
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k k'))))).IsEquivalence :=
  isEquivalence_finiteEtaleBaseChange_specMap_algebraMap_of_properHenselian f h0A48 fun P =>
    have : IsProper (P.hom ≫ f) := isProper_comp_of_finiteEtaleOver f P
    finiteEtaleDescendsToHenselianPoint_of_isAlgClosed (P.hom ≫ f)

end Descent

end AlgebraicGeometry

